    definition: 'Selection sort partitions an array into a sorted prefix and unsorted suffix. Each pass selects the smallest suffix value and exchanges it with the first suffix position.',
    plain: 'Find the smallest remaining card before you move anything. Put it in the next empty final position. Repeat with the cards still waiting.',
    idea: 'The scan proves which value belongs at index i; one swap puts it there. A new smaller candidate updates an index during the scan rather than causing an immediate swap.',
