    invariant: 'Before pass i, positions 0..i-1 contain the i smallest values in final order. During the scan, min names the smallest value seen from i through j.',
    costs: [['Best / average / worst', 'O(n²)', 'Every suffix is fully scanned, even on sorted input.'], ['Key comparisons', 'n(n - 1)/2', 'Lengths n - 1, n - 2, ... , 1.'], ['Swaps', 'At most n - 1', 'At most one actual exchange per pass; self-swaps are skipped.'], ['Auxiliary space', 'O(1) iterative; O(n) recursive', 'Only index variables and a temporary value in the iterative form.'], ['Stable / in place / adaptive', 'No / yes / no', 'A long swap can cross equal records; scanning does not shrink with presortedness.']],
    descending: 'Select the maximum instead: change arr[j] < arr[min] to arr[j] > arr[min]. The prefix then grows in descending order.',
    mistakes: [['Set min = arr[i]', 'Treats a value as an index.', 'Set min = i, then compare arr[j] and arr[min].'], ['Swap every new minimum immediately', 'Changes the taught selection procedure and swap counts.', 'Finish the full scan, then swap once.'], ['Always swap min and i', 'Adds redundant writes when they are the same.', 'Skip the swap when min == i.'], ['Call it stable', 'Long-distance exchanges can cross equal values.', 'Use a tagged duplicate counterexample.']],
